# Module Contracts

Create a `MOD-*.md` contract only for a durable multi-file boundary whose scope is supported by an existing repository path, an explicit `dev/harness.toml` source/test path, or a confirmed planned path in an active product specification.

Do not create one contract per directory. A contract records only explicit ownership, responsibility, applicable paths, public entry points, dependency rules, organization, and verification commands. Use `unknown` when evidence is unavailable rather than guessing.

Copy `_template.md`, choose a stable `MOD-*` ID, and run `./dev/code-map` followed by `./dev/docs-check`. The generated code map is a non-authoritative routing aid; this contract and the underlying source remain authoritative.
